From 7a5891e6561e720e735103deb35c17e4b2d9fbfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:38:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/26] Replace OBS product naming in app prompts; hide
 upstream-only menu items

Load optional locale/overrides/<lang>.ini files after the regular locale
so LiveHime can rename the running application in prompts (already
running, crash/safe mode, exit confirmation, macOS permissions, restart
notices, hide-from-capture) without touching upstream translation files.
OBS credits, OBS plugins and imports from OBS keep their wording.

The plugin hides upstream menu items that do not apply: updater, repair,
what's new, release notes, Discord, website, and uploading logs to OBS's
servers. A GetBrandingState automation request and e2e-branding.mjs
check both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
